        "---\n",
        "title: AI-Powered Patient Journey Analytics\n",
        "subtitle: An End-to-End GenAI Extraction Pipeline\n",
        "image: /assets/projects/ai-patient-journey/ai-patient-journey.png\n",
        "description: This project builds an end-to-end GenAI pipeline that transforms 50 synthetic IBD patient interview transcripts into structured, analyzable records using LLM-powered extraction with Pydantic schemas, chain-of-thought prompting, and confidence scoring. The pipeline combines classical NLP (TF-IDF, LDA/NMF topic modeling, VADER sentiment) with structured LLM extraction (Gemini 2.5 Flash via instructor + litellm) to answer four research questions about biologic treatment adoption, barriers, treatment patterns, and referral pathways.\n",
        "featured: 1\n",
        "category: GenAI\n",
        "type: NLP Pipeline\n",
        "skills:\n",
        "    - LiteLLM\n",
        "    - Instructor\n",
        "    - Pydantic\n",
        "    - Gemini API\n",
        "    - Scikit-Learn\n",
        "    - Pandas\n",
        "    - Plotly\n",
        "    - asyncio\n",
        "    - pytest\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "![]({{< meta image >}})\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key Findings\n",
        "\n",
        "- **68% of patients are currently on a biologic**, but churn bias suggests the true population rate is lower (55–65%).\n",
        "- **Cost and insurance (69%) is the dominant barrier** to biologic adoption — not clinical resistance. This co-occurs with nearly every other barrier.\n",
        "- **Median 3 treatment steps** before first biologic, following a consistent ladder: mesalamine → prednisone → immunomodulators → biologics.\n",
        "- **70% of patients were initially misdiagnosed** — most commonly as IBS or stress-related — navigating a median of 4 provider steps to established care.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Dataset\n",
        "\n",
        "The project uses 50 synthetic patient interview transcripts simulating clinical interviews with IBD patients. Each transcript is a first-person narrative covering diagnosis history, treatment sequences, biologic therapy experiences, insurance barriers, referral pathways, and emotional burden. The transcripts vary in length from ~1,000 to ~4,300 characters, with shorter transcripts potentially representing incomplete patient journeys (churn candidates).\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column-margin}\n",
        "![](/assets/projects/ai-patient-journey/corpus_statistics.png)\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "The dataset is stored as a JSON array where each entry contains a `patient_id` and an `interview_transcript`:"
      ],
      "id": "b6728d90"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| code-fold: false\n",
        "DATA_PATH = Path(\"../data/interviews.json\")\n",
        "\n",
        "with open(DATA_PATH) as f:\n",
        "    interviews = json.load(f)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pd.DataFrame(interviews)\n",
        "df[\"transcript_length\"] = df[\"interview_transcript\"].str.len()\n",
        "df[\"word_count\"] = df[\"interview_transcript\"].str.split().str.len()\n",
        "df[\"sentence_count\"] = df[\"interview_transcript\"].apply(lambda t: len(re.split(r\"[.!?]+\", t)))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Interviews loaded: {len(df)}\")\n",
        "df.iloc[:,-3:].describe()"
      ],
